    <h2>Why this is often harder than it sounds</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>If your limits were routinely overridden early on, the nervous system learned
        something practical: asserting a need costs more than absorbing the harm. That lesson
        does not expire on its own, and it does not respond to being told it is irrational.</p>
        <p>This is the territory
        <a href="/approach/narm/">NARM</a> works in, and it is why boundary trouble so often
        turns out to be developmental trauma wearing a practical disguise.</p>
